Problem Overview
Create and implement a turn-based combat simulator in which two monster teams battle until one side has no surviving monsters. A team owns an ordered collection of monsters, and every monster has hit points and an attack value. The teams act alternately, and the simulator must produce an event record for the entire fight.

This is an Object-Oriented Design exercise.


Part 1: Basic Battle System
Requirements
Build the battle system according to these rules:

Monster: Every monster includes:

A name used as a string identifier
Hit points (HP), represented by a positive integer
Attack strength, represented by a positive integer
Team: Every team contains:

Its team name
An ordered list of monsters
Battle Rules:

Team A takes the opening turn, after which the teams alternate turns.
During a turn, the attacking side's earliest living monster attacks the defending side's earliest living monster.
If monster A attacks monster B, apply B.health = B.health - A.attack.
The attacking monster takes no retaliatory damage.
A monster is removed from combat once its health is 0 or less.
Combat stops as soon as every monster on either team has been eliminated.
Event Log: Return a sequence of log entries that includes:

Every attack, including attacker, target, and damage amount
Each monster defeat
The final result, identifying the winning team
